<%# The answer to the autosave mint, and to a rename. The draft is real now, so
    everything the editor held back for a saved record arrives in place — Publish and its
    popover, the view button, Delete, the tag mint — without a reload and without moving
    the caret. A rename gets the same answer for the same reason: every one of these
    addresses the record, so a slug that moved leaves all of them pointing at a URL that
    no longer exists. Every action is an update into a slot the form already rendered
    empty, so each of these partials is the only place its markup exists. Shared with
    Writing::PagesController, which writes through the same form.

    Morphed, not replaced: on a new post this lands every couple of seconds while the
    title is still being typed, and rebuilding the nodes would drop the writer out of
    whatever he had open on top of them. Morphing keeps the nodes; it still reconciles
    away state the server can't know about, which is why autosave holds the open state
    across the render and why the two slots below are sent only by the mint. %>
<%= turbo_stream.update "editor-actions", method: :morph do %>
  <%= render "writing/posts/editor_actions", post: post %>
<% end %>
<%= turbo_stream.update "editor-overlays", method: :morph do %>
  <%= render "writing/posts/editor_overlays", post: post %>
<% end %>
<%# Only the mint has anything to say to these two: the Delete button reaches its form by
    the HTML form attribute and the tag mint names the post by id, so neither carries a URL
    a rename could stale. Sending them anyway would retype the writer's half-written tag
    name into an empty box every couple of seconds. %>
<% if post.previously_new_record? %>
  <%= turbo_stream.update "editor-delete" do %>
    <%= render "writing/posts/editor_delete", post: post %>
  <% end %>
  <% if post.taggable? %>
    <%= turbo_stream.update "editor-tag-mint" do %>
      <%= render "writing/posts/tag_mint", post: post %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
